# Text files are LF in the repo AND in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git-for-Windows default) materialises CRLF on checkout, and
# the QA gate breaks on any fresh clone or `git worktree add`: tools/qa/replay_login.js and
# replay_premium.js parse multi-line Swift string literals with `\` continuations and do not strip the
# `\r`, so ReplayLogin and ReplayPremium fail with 8 phantom string mismatches. The same files pass in a
# checkout whose Swift was written locally with LF — which is why this was invisible until the first
# worktree. It also stops `php tools/eco/build_eco.php` from dirtying eco.tsv and eco-data.js with
# line-ending-only diffs.
#
# The blobs in the repo are already LF, so this changes nothing that is committed — only what lands in
# the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.png    binary
*.webp   binary
*.mp3    binary
*.ttf    binary
*.sqlite binary
*.pdf    binary
